1. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: a person or thing which does the base word
Examples: (ABUSE) {2}, (OBSERVE) {3}, (CONSUME) {4}

2. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: to cause a person/thing to be in the place, state, or condition of the base word
Examples: (SURE) {2}

3. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: creates an adjective, tending to do or be like the base word
Examples: (REFLECT) {2}, (DECEIVE) {3}, (MASS) {4}, (COLLECT) {5}, (ABUSE) {6}

4. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: not the base word, the opposite of the base word
Examples: (ETHICAL) {2}, (AMUSED) {3}, (KIND) {4}

5. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: creates a noun; the act, practice, or process of doing something; an abnormal state or condition resulting from too much of the base word
Examples: (CONSUMER) {2}, (CRITIC) {3}, (DYNAMIC) {4}

6. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: badly, wrongly
Examples: (LEAD) {2}, (RULE) {3}

7. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: creates a noun; the state, condition, or quality of the base word
Examples: (KIND) {2}, (APPARENT) {3}, (CASUAL) {4}, (DELIBERATE) {5}

8. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: without, lacking
Examples: (AIM) {2}, (PASSION) {3}

9. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: creates a noun form; the action, process, or result of doing something
Examples: (AUMSE) {2}

10. Prefix/Suffix: {1}
Definition: creates an adjective; capable of, fit for, or worthy of the base word
Examples: (SUSTAIN) {2}, (CONSUME) {3}, (REPUTATION) {4}, (DISTINGUISH) {5}
